    "remote memory backends with real network latency"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The fake backend is a local HTTP server; real backend latency distributions are not measured here",
    "The microbenchmark ran on a loaded shared host; A/A is reported beside every delta",
    "Store drain uses relay_shared_metrics._reset_for_tests(), the same hook the upstream tests use",
    "holographic swallows its own errors and returns \"\", so a failing holographic recall reports as empty, not failed (provider behaviour, not the metric)"
  ],
